# Worker deploy reminder

Production account API traffic (lists, sync, friends, TMDB proxy, admin, movies batch) runs on the Cloudflare Worker. Localhost also hits the deployed Worker URL unless a dev-only fallback applies.

## Required in every completion summary

When the session changed anything that affects the Worker, **always** end the summary with a **Deploy** section. Do not skip it, even if the user did not ask.

If no Worker-affecting changes were made, omit the section.

## When a Worker deploy is required

Treat these as needing `wrangler deploy`:

- Any edit under `worker/` (including `worker/src/`, tests that imply production behavior, `wrangler.toml`)
- Any edit under `scripts/lib/` for a module listed in `scripts/sync-worker-lib.js` (`lists`, `friend-activity`, `list-query`, `sort`, etc.) — run `npm run sync-worker-lib` first, then deploy
- D1 schema/migration changes referenced by the Worker

Static-only changes (`css/`, `js/app/` UI with no synced lib change, `data/posters/`, `server.js`) do **not** require wrangler. They may need a static site deploy instead.

## What to tell the user

Use this exact command unless the README documents a different flow:

```bash
cd worker && wrangler deploy
```

Also mention when relevant:

- Run `npm run sync-worker-lib` before deploy if `scripts/lib/` synced modules changed
- Production picks up API changes only after deploy; static `npm run build` alone is not enough for Worker routes
- Optional: static/Netlify deploy if frontend bundle changed too

## Example summary footer

**Deploy:** These changes hit the account API. From the repo root:

```bash
npm run sync-worker-lib   # if scripts/lib synced modules changed
cd worker && wrangler deploy
```

Reload the site after deploy (friend activity polls ~60s).
